==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Crazed Sexy Legs Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Manic Macho Legs''' when obtained from [[Muscle Party (Deadly)|Gross Maniac]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Crazed Gross Cat makes up for its increased recharge time with the ability to produce [[Wave Attack|Wave]] attacks, giving it a surprisingly large pseudo-AOE to easily clear peons for single-target attackers.

Crazed Gross Cat finds even more use in stages with enemies that have high range, such as [[THE SLOTH]], [[Camelle]], or [[Calamary]], as the [[Wave Attack|Wave]] attacks will hit enemies far beyond its target and deal damage to them. Aside from its combat abilities, Crazed Sexy Legs Cat can be used in conjunction with regular [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]] to activate the [[Legs for Days (Combo)|Legs For Days]] [[Cat Combo]], which slightly increases knockback, as well as the [[Gross!!! (Combo)|Gross!!!]] combo with [[Marshmallow Cat (Rare Cat)|Marshmallow Cat]], which increases freeze duration, essential to strategies involving relevant crowd-controlling units.

==='''True Form'''===
Manic Macho Legs has slightly more health and longer [[Wave Attack]]s. The health is a small improvement, but the Wave Attack augment is exceptional as this allows the unit to hit many more enemy backliners from a safe distance. An example would be the [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cats]] in [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 28|Floor 28]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]], which can be somewhat easily defeated by stacking Manic Macho Legs on the metal enemies as the wave has just enough reach to hit them.

